  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.19\"\n\npackage:\n  name: cigetcert\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/c/cigetcert/cigetcert-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: db7c3226552d23516aa16a767dfce8031362640fc7a94d87a0a6e90d5c8afb36\n\nbuild:\n  number: 6\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . --no-build-isolation --no-deps -vv\n  skip:\n    - win\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - pip\n    - python\n    - setuptools\n  run:\n    - python\n    - lxml\n    - m2crypto\n    - pyopenssl\n    - if: win\n      then: winkerberos\n      else: pykerberos\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      files:\n        - if: unix\n          then: share/man/man1/cigetcert.1\n  - script:\n      - cigetcert --listinstitutions\n      - if: unix\n        then: if command -v man; then man -P cat cigetcert; fi\n\nabout:\n  summary: Get an X.509 certificate with SAML ECP and store proxies\n  description: |\n    cigetcert gets an X.509 certificate from a SAML 2.0 Service Provider\n    (SP) such as CILogon using the Enhanced Client or Proxy (ECP)\n    profile. Optionally it can also get a grid proxy certificate and/or\n    transfer a grid proxy to MyProxy. It was developed for the Fermilab\n    Distributed Computing Access with Federated Identities (DCAFI) project\n    but is intended to be usable by other projects.\n  homepage: https://cdcvs.fnal.gov/redmine/projects/fermitools/wiki/cigetcert\n  repository: https://github.com/fermitools/cigetcert\n  documentation: http://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://github.com/fermitools/cigetcert/blob/master/cigetcert.html\n  license: BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file: COPYING\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - duncanmmacleod\n",
